{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, טְאֵב","hw":"טְאֵב","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">טְאֵב</span></big>  <strong>vb. be good (</strong>𝔗 Syriac, v. BH <a data-ref=\"BDB, טוֹב²\" href=\"/BDB,_טוֹב²\", dir=\"rtl\">טוֹב</a><strong>)</strong>;—<br><strong>Pe.</strong>  Pf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">ט׳</span>, c. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל</span> pers. <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:24\" href=\"/Daniel.6.24\">Dn 6:24</a> <em>it was good to him</em> = <em>he was glad</em> (cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB Aramaic, בְּאֵשׁ\" href=\"/BDB Aramaic,_בְּאֵשׁ\", dir=\"rtl\">בְּאֵשׁ</a> v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:15\" href=\"/Daniel.6.15\">15</a>).","next":"BDB Aramaic, טָב","prev":"BDB Aramaic, חֲתַם"}